# P0 GATE LIBRARY (use these patterns only)

## 1) Boolean gate: pattern exists?
Use Select-String -Quiet and print ONLY PASS/FAIL:
Example:
  $hit = (command | Select-String -Pattern "..." -Quiet)
  if($hit){ "HIT" } else { "OK_EMPTY" }

## 2) Never use in PowerShell gates
- findstr
- 2>nul (cmd redirection)  -> use 2>$null
- $LASTEXITCODE for pipeline success/failure (unreliable with PowerShell cmdlets)
- Out-File / implicit Out-File to devices
- Formatting implicit objects when you only need PASS/FAIL

## 3) Audit output (only when required)
When output must list matches, force 1 match = 1 line:
  ... | Select-String -Pattern "..." |
  ForEach-Object { Write-Output ($_.Path + ':' + $_.LineNumber + ':' + $_.Line.Trim()) }

## 4) Ban dollar-dot
Never use dollar-dot (e.g. property on `$`). Only use `$_` or named vars.
